-- examples/checks/vscode-surface-split-check.rofl — vscode_surface_split: the side-effect question over the 19 files of
-- examples/vscode/mini and examples/vscode/split (facts in vscode-split-facts.rofl), every file resident, through the
-- [surface] book (rules/js-surface.rofl). Every answer named; red if one is missing or one more appears. The same facts
-- come out of each file evaluated ALONE with the others' [surface]: scripts/surface_split.ts (npm run test:split) is
-- that gate, and its planted break is the original model with no surface. The files, by node prefix:
--   mini/common/channels.ts n6329e4a1ce5a5737   split/app.ts       n34281c6d11fa17ac   split/guard.ts     n1757fbf66a95b84a
--   mini/node/main.ts       n6ce3b3e159e9764b   split/cb.ts        n4eee02055dfecceb   split/lib.ts       n2cab440d5303505d
--   mini/node/pfs.ts        nd100d8f9c1968a85   split/consumer.ts  n1684850c959c2a12   split/reexports.ts n7260e653f095f551
--   mini/node/server.ts     n34efd0fd49e79fa1   split/each.ts      n303f3c0ccfb1010a   split/store.ts     n346d69f15eaf6d53
--                                               split/errors.ts    n02a978cc9a4fd53e   split/util.ts      nd31751746bbd649e
--                                               split/parent.ts    nc8becf8b83426b75   split/child.ts     n868c94af7517458b
-- What each extra file is for:
--   a helper merged across callers   util.ts `id(p) { return p }` called from store.ts ('/var/a', '/var/b') and consumer.ts
--                                    (as `ident` through a re-export, '/etc/x'; as `u.id` through a namespace, '/var/c'):
--                                    each call has ITS argument, not the four (`sx_ret_param`); `ensure(dir)`, a sink inside
--                                    a helper, still has every caller's value (one caller here)
--   re-export and `export *`         reexports.ts `export { id as ident } from`, `export * from`
--   namespace, require, default      consumer.ts `import * as u`, `require('./util.js')`; store.ts `import home`
--   a member written from elsewhere  consumer.ts `u.settings.mode = 'slow'` is read by util.ts flush(): 'fast' and 'slow'
--   a callback over another array    cb.ts `each(['/tmp/a1', '/tmp/a2'], p => fs.unlinkSync(p))`; each.ts iterates and calls
--   a throw caught elsewhere         errors.ts fail() throws, guard.ts catches it: caught_value, no catch_from_host
--   a callee placed by its callers   lib.ts helper() is called unguarded only from app.ts: reached, not may_not_run;
--                                    the arrow in cb.ts is called only inside each.ts's loop: may_not_run
--   a path built in another file     locations.ts n3ea02c0aa5d7188d, writer.ts ndc27e34f71d5ff1f: LOGS, an
--                                    exported template; cacheFile(name), a returned path.join; withExt(base), a `+` whose
--                                    part is writer.ts's template; LOGS + '/all.log' in writer.ts over the imported template.
--                                    Each answers with its node and its text (rules/js-concat.rofl), and mini/node/paths.ts
--                                    with the texts and nodes of examples/checks/vscode-side-effects-check.rofl
--   an imported class                app.ts `new Registry()` of lib.ts's `export class`: Registry.open's mkdirSync and the
--                                    call `r.open('/srv/data')` both answer '/srv/data'
--   an override from another file    child.ts CleanJob extends parent.ts's Job: Job.run's `this.step()` is CleanJob's
--                                    instance there too, so it reaches CleanJob.step and its rmSync('/srv/old')
--   no value                         main.ts remove(this.storage.dir)
